  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Sector Humanitarian Response for Conflict-Affected Persons in Northern Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since October 2017, non-state armed groups have targeted civilians in Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique using violence, killings, kidnappings, abductions, destruction, and looting of public and private property. In total, there are an estimated 1.5 million people in need, which includes 946,508 internally displaced persons. 
 
To address the effects of violence and insecurity in northern Mozambique, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing humanitarian aid to conflict-affected persons &#x2013; especially internally displaced persons, host communities, and those left behind &#x2013; while reducing and responding to vulnerabilities and threats. IOM is delivering primary healthcare services through mobile and static clinics, while ensuring community-based health services through a network of activists and community health workers. For continuous and critical information on displacement numbers and trends as well as the needs of conflict-affected persons, IOM is implementing Displacement Tracking Matrix systems to collect and analyse data. Moreover, a crisis modifier is included to respond to a potential crisis caused by natural hazards or other shocks, including epidemics and disease outbreaks.</narrative>
  </description>
